sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant S as Sender
    participant X as Relays and STUN
    participant R as Receiver

    Note over S,R: 1 · Pairing
    S-->>R: QR code: 32 random bytes, by camera
    S->>X: join the derived room, on every network at once
    R->>X: join the derived room, on every network at once
    X-->>S: the peer and its session description, sealed with the code
    X-->>R: the peer and its session description, sealed with the code
    S->>X: STUN: what is my public address?
    R->>X: STUN: what is my public address?
    Note over S,R: ICE settles a route (local, direct, or TURN) and the WebRTC data channel opens
    S->>R: ECDH public key
    R->>S: ECDH public key

    Note over S,R: 2 · Verifying: four emoji, compared by the two people
    Note over S: They match

    Note over S,R: 3 · Negotiating, every message sealed, on the data channel
    S->>R: path verdict · lan-hello · quic-hello
    R->>S: path verdict · lan-hello · quic-hello, in reply
    R->>S: the listener's offer: addresses, port, token, answer
    S-->>R: dial the offer: token in, answer back
    S->>R: manifest: name and size
    Note over R: Accept
    R->>S: accept
    Note over S: the sender moves to the best route that is up, here and only here

    Note over S,R: 4 · Moving the file
    S->>R: sealed chunks, over LAN, QUIC or WebRTC
    R->>S: pause / resume, always on WebRTC
    S->>R: complete, with the file's digest
    R->>S: done

    Note over S,R: 5 · Leaving: a leave message, then every socket closes
